plaso-webhist.tsv, plaso-chrome-cache.tsv.gz, plaso-firefox-cache.tsv.gz:
what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads from plaso's
test files (tests/fixtures/plaso/, see its NOTICE) with its
sqlite/edge_load_statistics, binary_cookies, cookie plugins (Google
Analytics, through sqlite/chrome_17_cookies, sqlite/chrome_66_cookies,
sqlite/firefox_2_cookies, sqlite/firefox_10_cookies and binary_cookies),
opera_global, opera_typed_history, java_idx, chrome_cache, firefox_cache
and firefox_cache2 parsers (psort -a -o json_line), one line per event,
written by plaso_tsv.py (its docstring lists the columns). Written from
plaso's output, not from this crate.

The input layouts, on a host with Docker, the files as in plaso's
test_data/ at commit 91b6849503b125267d00ea134248e4fe59e5479c (whole
folders for the caches, with data_3, the f_ files and E8D65m01):

    /tmp/sbx/edge/in/load_statistics.db
    /tmp/sbx/ga/in/{cookies.db,Cookies-68.0.3440.106,firefox_2_cookies.sqlite,
                    firefox_10_cookies.sqlite,Cookies.binarycookies}
    /tmp/sbx/opera/in/{global_history.dat,typed_history.xml}
    /tmp/sbx/javaidx/in/{java.idx,java_602.idx}
    /tmp/sbx/chromecache/in/{chrome_cache,chrome_cache_v3}/
    /tmp/sbx/firefoxcache/in/{cache2,firefox28,firefox3}/ and invalid_file

For each <set> and its parsers:

    edge          sqlite/edge_load_statistics
    ga            sqlite/chrome_17_cookies,sqlite/chrome_66_cookies,sqlite/firefox_2_cookies,sqlite/firefox_10_cookies,binary_cookies
    opera         opera_global,opera_typed_history
    javaidx       java_idx
    chromecache   chrome_cache
    firefoxcache  firefox_cache,firefox_cache2

the commands:

    sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/sbx/<set>:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 log2timeline --status_view none -q --parsers '<parsers>' --storage-file /data/out.plaso /data/in
    sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/sbx/<set>:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 psort --status_view none -q -a -o json_line -w /data/out.jsonl /data/out.plaso

then, the four first sets' out.jsonl joined into webhist.jsonl:

    python3 -I tests/oracle/plaso_tsv.py webhist.jsonl > tests/oracle/plaso-webhist.tsv
    python3 -I tests/oracle/plaso_tsv.py chromecache.jsonl | gzip -9n > tests/oracle/plaso-chrome-cache.tsv.gz
    python3 -I tests/oracle/plaso_tsv.py firefoxcache.jsonl | gzip -9n > tests/oracle/plaso-firefox-cache.tsv.gz

plaso_tsv.py keeps the data types it lists only: of the ga set, Safari's
cookies and the Google Analytics events (Chromium's and Firefox's cookies
are in plaso-extras.tsv).

The *.visits files are written by gen.sh (see it); plaso-extras.tsv from
plaso's output for the cookie, form history, extension and Safari parsers.
